#~ The template of every TOC the package carries.  Lines starting with #~ are notes about the template
#~ and are left out of the TOCs.  build.py fills the {{...}} lines from games.py, once per shipped game:
#~   {{interface}}    ## Interface
#~   {{notes}}        that game's ## Notes lines
#~   {{game-header}}  lines only that game's TOC has (AllowLoadGameType for Mists of Pandaria Classic)
#~   {{zone-data}}    that game's zone tables
#~   {{data}}         that game's database: the generated data and the override files
#~ PandaQuest/PandaQuest.toc is written from here and kept in the repository, because CurseForge's own
#~ packager reads it as it is.  Edit this file, never that one, then run
#~   python3 .github/release/build.py tocs
#~ check.py fails while the two differ.
## Interface: {{interface}}
## Title: |cff5fd7ffPanda|rQuest
{{notes}}
# The series only.  What ships is 0.2.<commits on this repository's main>, computed at package time
# and stamped into this file and into ## Title (build.py: release_version, stamp_toc); a third
# component written down here would be one nobody remembers to bump.
## Version: 0.2.0
## Author: vem882
# PandaQuestAH stays although the Auction module is gone: WoW deletes a SavedVariable that is no
# longer listed here at the next logout, and a player's stored auction scans must not be lost.
# Nothing reads or writes it any more.
## SavedVariables: PandaQuestDB, PandaQuestSync, PandaQuestAH, PandaQuestProf
## OptionalDeps: TomTom, Questie, QuestieDB
## IconTexture: Interface\AddOns\PandaQuest\Textures\icon.tga
## X-Website: https://github.com/vem882/pandaquest
## X-License: GPL-3.0
# Release channel: stable. Write beta here to ship a beta (README.md, "The release channel").
## X-Release-Channel: stable
## X-Curse-Project-ID: 1735809
## X-Wago-ID: n6VYMQNd
{{game-header}}
# Category is set because Questie sets it, and "Quests" is Questie's own value, so if the client
# does group by it a player with both installed finds them under one heading.  What 5.5.4 actually
# does with the field is NOT verified: the only AddOns-list source in the reference trees
# (Blizzard_AddOnList/Classic_AddonList.lua) builds one flat list from C_AddOns.GetAddOnInfo and
# never reads Category, and no Blizzard TOC in those trees declares it.
# X-Category stays beside it: nothing here reads it either, but it is the TOC's namespace for
# third-party metadata and dropping it would be silent.
## Category: Quests
